60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Given the clay subsoil and phasing limits, a wetland plan might be too risky for the earth-moving.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The drainage issues support a wetland approach, but the heat readings suggest we need shade, not just water.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,"The volunteer groups could help with habitat tasks, but the professional roll is too small for a complex wetland.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Minako,,The basin success shows water works. But the tree failure shows we need a plan with lower maintenance demands.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The fund only covers planting and water. A wetland plan fits the funding, but the upkeep cost is triple.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Jonathan, if the upkeep is triple, can the city afford it long-term?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the people use firm ground. A wetland with boardwalks might not match their behavior.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Minako, if the trees died, will the reed beds survive? I am worried about the aftercare.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, reed beds are different from trees. They are more resilient if the water is managed well.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the fund terms are the biggest constraint. We cannot build the plaza or terraces.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"The sports terraces require hard surfacing, which the fund does not cover. That is a dead end.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,The market plaza also needs hard surfacing and buildings. It is not viable with the current funding.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,"The woodland walk is dense planting. The upkeep cost would be very high, and the trees might die.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Minako,,The wetland restoration uses the fund correctly. It addresses the drainage issues and uses the basin success.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"The wetland plan is the only one that fits the fund terms. The high upkeep is a risk, but the others are impossible.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I am concerned about the earth-moving, but the other plans are not fundable. I will vote for the wetland.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,The drainage data supports the wetland. It is the most logical choice given the constraints.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I hope the volunteers can help. I will vote for the wetland, as it is the only one that fits the budget.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Minako,,The basin success is a good sign. I will vote for the wetland restoration.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,The fund terms force this choice. I will vote for the wetland restoration.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
